5.1 The pattern
A connected component is a maximal set of vertices that can all reach each other. In G1 there are
two: {1,2,3,4,5,6} and {7,8}. The pattern for anything about components is four lines you already saw:
int comps = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
if (!vis[i]) {
comps++;
dfs(i); // or bfs(i)
}
}
Every time the loop finds an unvisited vertex, that vertex belongs to a component nobody has touched
yet, so we increment and explore all of it. When the loop ends, every vertex has been visited exactly
once and comps is the answer. Use DFS or BFS, it makes no difference to the answer.

Usually you want to know which component a vertex is in, and how big
each one is.
